    "q-85324": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85324",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "An airport manager notes that, on average, $4$ planes each day are delayed by more than one hour. What is the probability that precisely $8$ planes will be delayed by more than one hour tomorrow? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that delays occur independently and at a constant average rate.",
      "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of airplanes that are delayed by more than one hour on a particular day. Since the average rate is $4$ delayed airplanes per day, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, $X$ can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =4,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(4).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{4}^{x}{e}^{-4}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of precisely $8$ airplanes will be delayed on any particular day is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=8) & =f(8) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{8}{e}^{-4}}{8!} \\\\  & ≈0.030\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
