    "q-85251": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85251",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "A writer is editing the first draft of a book. On average, there have been $4$ typos per page. What is the probability of finding fewer than $4$ typos on the next page? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that typos occur independently and at a constant average rate.",
      "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of typos on a page of the book. Since the average rate is $4$ typos per page, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of typos can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =4,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(4).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{4}^{x}{e}^{-4}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding fewer than $4$ typos on the next page is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{0}{e}^{-4}}{0!}+\\frac{{4}^{1}{e}^{-4}}{1!}+\\frac{{4}^{2}{e}^{-4}}{2!}+\\frac{{4}^{3}{e}^{-4}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.433\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
