      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The Philippines is subject to tropical cyclones, with a month-round average frequency of $2.5$ typhoons per month. What is the probability that there will be no more than $2$ typhoons next month? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that typhoons occur independently and at a constant average rate.",
      "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of typhoons in a month in the Philippines. Since the average rate is $2.5$ typhoons per month, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of typhoons can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =2.5,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(2.5).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{2.5}^{x}{e}^{-2.5}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that there will be at most $2$ typhoons next month is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2.5}^{0}{e}^{-2.5}}{0!}+\\frac{{2.5}^{1}{e}^{-2.5}}{1!}+\\frac{{2.5}^{2}{e}^{-2.5}}{2!} \\\\  & ≈0.544\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
