    "q-85253": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85253",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "A writer is editing the first draft of a book. On average, there have been $2$ typos per page. What is the probability of finding at least $4$ typos on the next page? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that typos occur independently and at a constant average rate.",
      "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of typos on a page of the book. Since the average rate is $2$ typos per page, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of typos can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =2,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(2).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{2}^{x}{e}^{-2}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X\\ge 4),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 4)=1-P(X<4)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in {0,1,2,3}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{0}{e}^{-2}}{0!}+\\frac{{2}^{1}{e}^{-2}}{1!}+\\frac{{2}^{2}{e}^{-2}}{2!}+\\frac{{2}^{3}{e}^{-2}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.857\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding at least $4$ typos on the next page is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 4) & =1-P(X<4) \\\\  & ≈1-0.857 \\\\  & =0.143\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
